w: 1.~God is our re- fuge and our strength, Our ev- er pre- sent aid, And there- fore, though the earth re- move, We will not be a- fraid; Though hills a- mid the seas be cast, Though foa- ming wa- ters roar, Yea, though the might- y bil- lows shake The moun- tains on the shore.
w: 2.~A ri- ver flows whose streams make glad The ci- ty of our God, The ho- ly place where- in the Lord Most High has His a- bode; Since God is in the midst of her, Un- moved her walls shall stand, For God will be her ear- ly help, When trou- ble is at hand.
w: 3.~The na- tions raged, the king- doms moved, But when His voice was heard The troub- led earth was stilled to peace Be- fore His might- y word. The Lord of Hosts is on our side, Our safe- ty to se- cure; The God of Ja- cob is for us A re- fuge strong and sure.
w: 4.~O come, be- hold what won- drous works Je- ho- vah's hand has wrought; Come, see what de- so- la- tion great He on the earth has brought. To ut- most ends of all the earth He caus- es war to cease; The wea- pons of the strong de- stroyed, He makes a- bid- ing peace.
w: 5.~Be still and know that I am God, O'er all ex- alt- ed high; The sub- ject na- tions of the earth My Name shall mag- ni- fy. The Lord of Hosts is on our side, Our safe- ty to se- cure, The God of Ja- cob is for us A re- fuge strong and sure.
